+  // finally, we choose R >= alpha / beta, where alpha is the bound on the
+  // ks-added noise. for power-of-2 m, we have:
+  // alpha = qKS^(1/c)*c*phim*sqrt(ln(phim))*P*sigma*k/sqrt(12)
